  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>\"4-Methyl\" indicates that there is a methyl group (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>) attached to the fourth carbon atom.</p><p>\"Pent-2-enal\" indicates that there is an aldehyde functional group (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>─</mo><mi>CHO</mi></math>) attached to the  five-carbon chain, and there is a double bond (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>─</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>─</mo></math>) between the second and third carbon atoms.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0126_85ddf5d50ffa.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 157px;\"/></p>"
